    "result_text": "The build passes with all tests green.\n\nSummary of the change \u2014 I implemented a case-insensitive email-uniqueness check on owner creation, mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern rather than duplicating logic:\n\n- **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 declared `existsByEmailIgnoreCase(String email)` alongside `existsByTelephone`. The Spring Data JPA repository picks this up as a derived query automatically (`IgnoreCase` \u2192 lower-cased comparison).\n- **`JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`** / **`JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`** \u2014 implemented it with `LOWER(email) = LOWER(:email)` count queries, matching each impl's existing style.\n- **`ClinicService` / `ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 added `ownerExistsWithEmail`, delegating to the repository under `@Transactional(readOnly = true)`, exactly like the telephone method.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a conflict check right after the telephone check that returns `409 CONFLICT` when the email is already used (case-insensitively), guarding against a null email since that column is optional.\n\nThe `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test passes, and the pre-existing suite stays green.",
